(SECTION: AiTC contact strategy. What this document is. This is the AGI Aeronautics marketing) Tj
T*
(and first-contact strategy for AiTC. It describes the product, how to write the first email,) Tj
T*
(how to follow up when there is no reply, how to follow up when there is a reply, how to ask) Tj
T*
(for a trial, and how the licence is structured. AGI Aeronautics confirms any price in a) Tj
T*
(written proposal. This document does not set a public price.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Browser radar and tower. AiTC runs both radar simulations and tower) Tj
T*
(simulations directly in the browser. A training session can start on the hardware that is) Tj
T*
(already in the room. The same exercise can be opened from another location without) Tj
T*
(installing a separate simulator application for that operating system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Hardware and operating system. AiTC is hardware-agnostic. It does not) Tj
T*
(depend on one operating system. An academy, a university, or an air navigation service can) Tj
T*
(run an exercise on the computers it already has, because the simulation is delivered in the) Tj
T*
(browser.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Airspace creation. Airspace is created inside AiTC. It can be drawn) Tj
T*
(manually, or it can be created with the artificial intelligence in the platform. The source) Tj
T*
(can be a file from another simulator, an aeronautical information publication, or another) Tj
T*
(file that contains the airspace information. An entire country airspace can be created) Tj
T*
(within minutes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Exercise creation and preview. Exercises are created inside AiTC. The) Tj
T*
(exercise-creation module can preview the exercise before it is used in training. The person) Tj
T*
(creating the exercise can test it and plan the exact traffic picture they want.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Exercise assistant. During exercise creation, an artificial) Tj
T*
(intelligence assistant accepts voice commands and text commands. A creator can ask for a) Tj
T*
(number of aircraft on a specific route, or for particular aircraft types. The creator can) Tj
T*
(then adjust by hand where the conflicts occur and where the traffic peak is.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Traffic load. For an exercise, AiTC can show the traffic that flows) Tj
T*
(through each sector in that exercise. The creator can see the volume of traffic, or the) Tj
T*
(traffic load, in those sectors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Aircraft scripts. Inside the exercise-creation module, scripts can) Tj
T*
(make aircraft carry out actions by themselves. The aircraft follow the script automatically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. AI piloting. AiTC can also use scripts for artificial intelligence) Tj
T*
(piloting. The aircraft can be piloted by the artificial intelligence, so a human) Tj
T*
(pseudo-pilot is not required at the other end of the exercise.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Replay. Training sessions can be recorded and played back in the) Tj
T*
(replay module. The playback is not a video recording and it is not an audio recording. It is) Tj
T*
(a scripted recording that reproduces the exercise from the start. Because a script recording) Tj
T*
(is a hundred times smaller, and more, than a video recording, a large number of exercises) Tj
T*
(can be stored.) Tj
T*
() Tj
