(SECTION: AiTC product. Voice and video. Voice communication runs in the browser. Users who) Tj
T*
(are connected to the same session can use simulated ground-to-air lines and ground-to-ground) Tj
T*
(lines. The voice system also supports video calling. In remote training, the instructor can) Tj
T*
(see the trainee during the session.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC product. Flight envelope. The aircraft database uses a detailed flight) Tj
T*
(envelope for each aircraft. Aircraft speed and altitude are not taken from a simple value) Tj
T*
(table. The aircraft in the simulation follows that flight-envelope model. A student can open) Tj
T*
(the flight-envelope graphic inside the simulation and see the limitations of the aircraft.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC first contact. Who receives the email. Write to the published institutional) Tj
T*
(mailbox for that organisation. Use the email stored on the outreach map. Do not write to a) Tj
T*
(named personal mailbox when the directory gives an office, enquiry, or training mailbox. One) Tj
T*
(organisation receives one first email.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC first contact. Subject and opening. The subject names AiTC and the) Tj
T*
(organisation. The first paragraph says that the sender is AGI Aeronautics and that AiTC is a) Tj
T*
(browser air traffic control simulator for radar and tower training. Do not claim that a) Tj
T*
(meeting is already arranged. Do not claim that the organisation has already agreed to) Tj
T*
(anything.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC first contact. One relevant capability. The second paragraph names one) Tj
T*
(capability that matches the recipient. For an academy or university, that can be exercise) Tj
T*
(creation, preview, and artificial intelligence piloting so a human pseudo-pilot is not) Tj
T*
(required. For an air navigation service, that can be creating their airspace from their own) Tj
T*
(files, including an aeronautical information publication, within minutes. Keep the email) Tj
T*
(short.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC first contact. The ask. Close by asking for a short conversation about a) Tj
T*
(trial. Offer to show radar and tower in the browser, on hardware they already use. Sign the) Tj
T*
(message as AGI Aeronautics. The mailbox signature is added when the message is sent from the) Tj
T*
(outbox.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC follow-up when there is no reply. Wait several working days after the first) Tj
T*
(email. Send one follow-up that refers to the first message and repeats the trial offer in) Tj
T*
(fewer words. If there is still no reply, send one second follow-up and then stop. Do not) Tj
T*
(write that they asked for a proposal. Do not invent a deadline they agreed to.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION: AiTC follow-up when they reply. Answer the question they asked. If they ask about) Tj
T*
(hardware, say that AiTC runs in the browser and does not depend on a particular operating) Tj
T*
(system. If they ask about airspace, say that airspace can be created in the platform from) Tj
T*
(their files and that a country airspace can be created within minutes. If they ask about) Tj
T*
(instructors in another location, say that the browser voice system includes video, so the) Tj
T*
(instructor can see the trainee during a remote session.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
